<section
  class="rules-section"
  id="nine-arena-rules"
  aria-labelledby="nine-rules-heading"
>
  <div class="home-section-head">
    <div>
      <span class="small-label">THE RULEBOOK</span><h2 id="nine-rules-heading">
        A fair fight. <em>An open record.</em>
      </h2>
    </div>
  </div><div class="rules-grid">
    <div>
      <span class="rule-number">01</span><h3>A decade earns the frame.</h3><p>
        The main rank uses 10-year annualized return minus SPY. Five-year form
        and one-year season badges tell the rest of the story.
      </p>
    </div><div>
      <span class="rule-number">02</span><h3>The same starting line.</h3><p>
        Matched dates. Reinvested distributions. Fund returns after expenses.
        Every card names the vehicle actually being measured.
      </p>
    </div><div>
      <span class="rule-number">03</span><h3>Rarity follows the record.</h3><p>
        Ten verified years qualify for the main arena. Shorter records belong in
        a separate division. Missing or uncertain data stays Unrated.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div><div
    class="rarity-scale"
    aria-label="Proposed 10-year investor rarity thresholds"
  >
    <span class="small-label"
      >10Y RARITY<br /> <small>ANNUALIZED GAP VS SPY</small></span
    ><span data-tier="legendary"
      ><i></i><b>Legendary</b><small>≥3 pp / year</small></span
    ><span data-tier="epic"
      ><i></i><b>Epic</b><small>1 to &lt;3 pp / year</small></span
    ><span data-tier="rare"
      ><i></i><b>Rare</b><small>0 to &lt;1 pp / year</small></span
    ><span data-tier="common"
      ><i></i><b>Common</b><small>Below 0 pp / year</small></span>
  </div><details class="scoring-details">
    <summary>Full grading rules and benchmark designation</summary><p>
      These are SPX Arena’s proposed performance tiers, not statistical proof of
      skill or risk-adjusted grades. The 5Y badge uses the same annualized
      thresholds. The 1Y season uses Legendary ≥10 pp, Epic ≥4 and &lt;10 pp,
      Rare ≥0 and &lt;4 pp, and Common &lt;0 pp. A full 10-year record is
      required for the main rank; 5–9 years qualify only for a separate
      five-year division.
    </p><p>
      The S&amp;P 500 card’s Legendary status is a special benchmark
      designation. It is not an investor rating and has no leaderboard rank. SPX
      identifies the index; the return figures and comparisons use SPY ETF
      market-price total returns. SPIVA’s statistics compare active funds with
      the index itself.
    </p><p>
      All periods end December 31, 2025. Ten years starts December 31, 2015;
      five years starts December 31, 2020; one year starts December 31, 2024.
      Full-career results are separate from the main rank. Rounded source data
      can leave a badge Unrated when it falls too close to a threshold, as with
      PSH’s five-year result.
    </p>
  </details>
</section>
